  "claimBoundary": "Eight real Ordivon incidents, two DeepSeek model families, two replicas, one-call direct versus four-alternative variation. Candidate coverage is an exploratory secondary metric computed with the same frozen diagnosis rubric; it does not alter the preregistered primary joint outcome. No owner change or shared search/variation infrastructure is authorized.",
  "evaluatorResidualAudit": {
    "consequence": "Do not use test/joint scores alone to infer candidate-generation quality. The diagnosis and candidate-coverage results use the frozen diagnosis rubric and independently show no variation advantage.",
    "example": "Web outputs proposing strace/ENAMETOOLONG are plausibly discriminating yet fail the frozen historical-test phrase rubric. Primary rubric remains unchanged.",
    "testRubricNarrow": true
  },
  "evidence": {
