  "interpretation": {
    "hVariationSupportedByF8A": false,
    "independentVariantF8BEarned": false,
    "modelInteraction": "Flash shows isolated variation rescues (notably Harness token normalization) while Pro is generally as good or better with direct diagnosis and substantially better on several discriminating-test choices. There is no cross-model monotonic variation benefit.",
    "nextFalsifier": "Do not build multi-agent or branching variation machinery from F8A. Revisit variation only if a natural problem supplies evidence that the correct causal family is absent from a strong direct model across repeated attempts, or if an independent-variant design has a mechanism that avoids the selection/compliance costs observed here.",
    "reason": "Removing the closed cause menu does not reveal a candidate-generation advantage. On strict both-valid pairs, final diagnosis is 2 variation wins / 2 direct wins / 17 ties. Candidate-set oracle coverage is 4 variation wins / 6 direct wins / 11 ties. Variation also has worse structured validity (23/32 vs 28/32). The test rubric is conservative and misses some reasonable alternative tests, but the no-gain conclusion does not depend on that rubric.",
    "selectionObservation": "Two valid variation rows contain an oracle-matching mechanism in alternatives while the final diagnosis selects a different/abstaining answer, showing that extra candidates can move the bottleneck from generation to selection rather than solve it."
  },
